layout: layouts/tool.njk
toolSlug: week-number-calculator
title: "Week Number Calculator: What Week Is It? (ISO)"
description: "See today's ISO 8601 week number, find the week for any date, get the Monday to Sunday dates of a week, and check whether a year has 52 or 53 weeks."
permalink: /tools/week-number-calculator/
h1: "Week Number Calculator"
extraCss: "/tools/week-number-calculator/style.css"
quickAnswer: "ISO 8601 weeks start on Monday, and week 1 is the week that contains the year's first Thursday (equivalently, the week with January 4 in it). So 1 January 2026 is in 2026-W01, but 1 January 2027 is still in 2026-W53, and 30 December 2024 already belongs to 2025-W01. Most years have 52 ISO weeks; 2026 has 53."
formula:
  title: "ISO 8601 Week Number Rule"
  expression: "ISO week = ⌊(day of year of that week's Thursday − 1) ÷ 7⌋ + 1, in the year that contains that Thursday"
  explanation: "Find the Thursday of the date's Monday-to-Sunday week (add 4 minus the ISO weekday, where Monday is 1 and Sunday is 7). The year that Thursday falls in is the ISO week-year, and counting whole weeks from January 1 of that year gives the week number. A year has 53 ISO weeks when it starts on a Thursday, or is a leap year that starts on a Wednesday; December 28 is always in the last week."
  variables:
    - name: "ISO weekday"
      description: "Monday = 1, Tuesday = 2 … Sunday = 7. Written after the week, as in 2026-W44-6 for a Saturday."
    - name: "ISO week-year"
      description: "The year the week belongs to. It differs from the calendar year for a few days around 1 January."
    - name: "US week number"
      description: "A different convention: weeks start on Sunday and week 1 is the week containing January 1, so the numbers can differ from ISO by one."
workedExamples:
