    <section class="content-section">
      <h2>How Many Weeks Are in a Year?</h2>
      <p>Most years have 52 ISO weeks. A 53rd week appears when the year starts on a Thursday, or when a leap year starts on a Wednesday, because that is when the year contains 53 Thursdays. This happens 71 times in every 400 years, roughly every five or six years.</p>
      <div class="table-wrapper">
        <table class="table">
          <caption class="visually-hidden">ISO weeks per year, 2024 to 2032</caption>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">ISO year</th><th scope="col">Weeks</th><th scope="col">Week 1 starts</th><th scope="col">1 January is a</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>2024</td><td>52</td><td>Mon 1 Jan 2024</td><td>Monday</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2025</td><td>52</td><td>Mon 30 Dec 2024</td><td>Wednesday</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2026</td><td><strong>53</strong></td><td>Mon 29 Dec 2025</td><td>Thursday</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2027</td><td>52</td><td>Mon 4 Jan 2027</td><td>Friday</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2028</td><td>52</td><td>Mon 3 Jan 2028</td><td>Saturday</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2029</td><td>52</td><td>Mon 1 Jan 2029</td><td>Monday</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2030</td><td>52</td><td>Mon 31 Dec 2029</td><td>Tuesday</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2031</td><td>52</td><td>Mon 30 Dec 2030</td><td>Wednesday</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2032</td><td><strong>53</strong></td><td>Mon 29 Dec 2031</td><td>Thursday</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2>ISO vs US Week Numbers</h2>
      <p>The ISO system is used for business planning, manufacturing, logistics and government statistics across Europe and much of the world. Each week has exactly seven days and belongs to exactly one year, which makes week-based reports add up. The US convention is simpler to read off a wall calendar but produces partial weeks: week 1 can be a single Saturday, and a year can have 53 or even 54 numbered weeks.</p>
      <ul class="content-list">
        <li><strong>Planning across countries:</strong> say "ISO week" in emails and contracts, and include the week-year (2026-W53) to avoid ambiguity at year end.</li>
        <li><strong>Spreadsheets:</strong> use <code>ISOWEEKNUM</code> in Excel and Google Sheets for ISO weeks, or <code>WEEKNUM(date, 21)</code>, which also follows ISO 8601.</li>
        <li><strong>Code:</strong> JavaScript has no built-in week number, Python offers <code>date.isocalendar()</code>, and PostgreSQL has <code>extract(week from date)</code> with <code>isoyear</code> for the week-year.</li>
        <li><strong>HTML forms:</strong> the <code>&lt;input type="week"&gt;</code> field uses the ISO format, such as 2026-W44.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
